//chromium-review.googlesource.com/329513 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ilja Friedel &lt;ihf@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="329513" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/portage-stable" ref="refs/changes/13/329513/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I64bafc0be9c83ccf4b4811deb0d7454de8e99775" commit="d84b84952dd465ad0d76118aab7d012adb9e0b80" commit_message="power: Add support for &quot;display off&quot; mode with keyboard wakeup  This patch adds a new operating mode to powerd's WakeupController: in addition to laptop, tablet and docked (external display with lid closed) we now have &quot;display off&quot; (external display with lid open but display brightness at 0). This mode is useful to use a Chromebook as a &quot;smart keyboard&quot;, in tablet configuration with the internal screen facing the table.  It's natural to use the keyboard to wake up the device after idle suspend in this mode. However, keyboard wakeup is gated by the EC which tries to prevent &quot;accidental&quot; key presses from waking up the device in tablet mode. Since the EC cannot know that the device has an external display attached and is not used as a tablet (despite the lid-angle), powerd has to disable this feature via MOTIONSENSE_CMD_KB_WAKE_ANGLE (using a maximum wake angle of 360 effectively disables angle-based wakeup inhibition completely).  BUG=chromium:552049 TEST=Played with Minnie in all the different configurations (lid angle above or below 180, with or without external display, backlight on or off) and confirmed that wakeup policy was as intended. Built with FEATURES=test for Falco.  Change-Id: I64bafc0be9c83ccf4b4811deb0d7454de8e99775 Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329948 Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329948" owner_email="jwerner@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/48/329948/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I8b6feaca9ca65aa76f4fa585621ae82ed7be839c" commit="75ee597d92a8e958be16bac06aaf4b2d4df6655b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: Set energy_aware if cpu energy model is available  In case CONFIG_SCHED_DEBUG is set, energy_aware is set by enabling the ENERGY_AWARE sched feature; otherwise it's set by toggling the energy_aware bool variable.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44828 TEST=Boot kernel on Oak.  Change-Id: I8b6feaca9ca65aa76f4fa585621ae82ed7be839c Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/296882 Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="296882" owner_email="jcliang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="27" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/82/296882/27" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I734df2058256c79b7bebc8ed324bbff04a605460" commit="af79398cf5f5d7ca6ffe2c64616875eb0b84647a" commit_message="Test to capture performance data from CFM device  This test enrolls ChromeOS device into hotrod mode and captures device usage data including cpu, memory and temperature data and uploads it to Google Cloud Storage as part of the test logs.  BUG=chromium:591257 TEST=Tested on local setup.  Change-Id: I734df2058256c79b7bebc8ed324bbff04a605460 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329965 Commit-Ready: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: harpreet Grewal &lt;harpreet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rohit Makasana &lt;rohitbm@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mats Nilsson &lt;mnilsson@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="329965" owner_email="harpreet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/65/329965/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic08b1c9362b26d6ca8d689f0e4eca836ec547293" commit="496e4263d6b22d992273d9a0414f799313760a89" commit_message="UPSTREAM: tracing/filter: Do not allow infix to exceed end of string  While debugging a WARN_ON() for filtering, I found that it is possible for the filter string to be referenced after its end. With the filter:   # echo '&gt;' &gt; /sys/kernel/debug/events/ext4/ext4_truncate_exit/filter  The filter_parse() function can call infix_get_op() which calls infix_advance() that updates the infix filter pointers for the cnt and tail without checking if the filter is already at the end, which will put the cnt to zero and the tail beyond the end. The loop then calls infix_next() that has   ps-&gt;infix.cnt--;  return ps-&gt;infix.string[ps-&gt;infix.tail++];  The cnt will now be below zero, and the tail that is returned is already passed the end of the filter string. So far the allocation of the filter string usually has some buffer that is zeroed out, but if the filter string is of the exact size of the allocated buffer there's no guarantee that the charater after the nul terminating character will be zero.  Luckily, only root can write to the filter.  Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org # 2.6.33+ Signed-off-by: Steven Rostedt &lt;rostedt@goodmis.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 6b88f44e161b9ee2a803e5b2b1fbcf4e20e8b980) Signed-off-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:591102 TEST=kernel builds  Change-Id: Ic08b1c9362b26d6ca8d689f0e4eca836ec547293 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330194 Commit-Ready: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330194" owner_email="smbarber@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/94/330194/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib2e5f7f5e29f280835ae890148f5c3dd2504a2f9" commit="0ebe2ad1b8a49092924726f3ffda74ecda92723a" commit_message="fusb302: update driver for FUSB302B  Update pull-ups code Manage BIST Test Data bit  BUG=none BRANCH=none TEST=PD contract established with various devices  Signed-off-by: Joe Bauman &lt;joe.bauman@fairchildsemi.com&gt;  Change-Id: Ib2e5f7f5e29f280835ae890148f5c3dd2504a2f9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329034 Commit-Ready: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="329034" owner_email="joe.bauman@fairchildsemi.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/34/329034/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iac3c8c9ceb6e491282e1c950c05c2718668e91b4" commit="92a3d58c570d8c39b26aeee5ba56790e0a936061" commit_message="prebuilts: write binhost conf files in PublishUprev  This CL refactors MasterUploadPrebuiltsStage into a non-stage standalone class. Instead of calling this stage prior to CompletionStage (as the CQ currently does), the conf writing code is called in PublishUprev stage immediately before uprev and conf commits are pushed.  This CL is a squashed version of the refactoring stack ending in https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/330258/ plus any additional post-refactor fixes.  BUG=chromium:591471 TEST=cbuildbot --remote --buildbot --debug master-paladin with this CL  Change-Id: Iac3c8c9ceb6e491282e1c950c05c2718668e91b4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330271 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Don Garrett &lt;dgarrett@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: David James &lt;davidjames@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="330271" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/71/330271/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Iff26dff720a169f4bdb85577abfd169f71ec5679" commit="8706f2bcefea69ac70c94b9ad5900dc27816e12d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: pinctrl: qcom: increase variable size for register offsets  On newer TLMM hardware blocks the registers are spread and we need an offsets upper than 16 bits to address them. Increase the register offset variables to 32 bits size.  Signed-off-by: Joonwoo Park &lt;joonwoop@codeaurora.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Stanimir Varbanov &lt;svarbanov@mm-sol.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bjorn Andersson &lt;bjorn.andersson@sonymobile.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Linus Walleij &lt;linus.walleij@linaro.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 981de1cb42306ebd94caa0d053a2b0ad47414043) Signed-off-by: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt;  Change-Id: Iff26dff720a169f4bdb85577abfd169f71ec5679 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/330259 Commit-Ready: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Tested-by: Sreedhar Sambangi &lt;ssambang@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_numbe